#import "/_lib/0.1.1.typ": *
#show: template

#taxon[Lemma]
#title[Identity type of cartesian decomposition]

Given a finite set $S$, we characterize the identity type of its cartesian decompositions as

$
&((A,B,e,p,q) =_"cart-dec"(S) (A',B',e',p',q'))\ 
~= &sum_(p: A ~= A', q : B ~= B') e' @ (p xx q) = e.
$

Here $(p xx q ) : (A xx B) ->  (A' xx B')$ denotes the induced map from the paths $p$ and $q$.

#proof[
  We make use of the #local("00EK")[Fundamental Theorem of Identity Types].

